# Annotated Markdown blocks: independent design review

Fixed inputs: Git base e6b05d3; exact source copies in snapshot.json. No production, specification or manuscript edits. This is design review plus independent Markdown parser observations, not validation of the future implementation.

Read directly: annotated.rs, shared projection Writer, Doc model/spec05/spec21, authoring, and actual authored00/01. The ordinary markdown() API is a separate restricted profile; changing shared helpers must not silently expand its domain.

Official references consulted:

- https://github.github.com/gfm/#tables-extension-
- https://github.github.com/gfm/#task-list-items-extension-
- https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#list-items
- https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#lists

GFM requires a header for a pipe table, trims cell edges, and has special escaped-pipe handling even inside code. CommonMark permits only nine-digit ordered markers. Consecutive same-marker lists can merge despite blank lines. Enable TABLES/TASKLISTS explicitly when checking this extended profile.

## Tables

Preserve column alignment (Default/Left/Center/Right), header presence, row order, exact cell counts and all annotation content. GFM's row padding/truncation cannot repair invalid typed Doc rows. Structural validation remains prior.

Doc permits header=None, zero columns, zero rows and empty Sentence cells. For an initial pipe-table profile, reject headerless and zero-column tables rather than promote data row0, invent a header or drop the table. A nonzero-column header-only table is representable; zero data rows alone are not a reason to reject it.

Allow empty Sentence/Text cells locally. Existing sentences() rejects empty visible output; do not relax paragraph/title or empty InlineCode rules globally. Empty cells are distinct from whitespace-only content which GFM trims. Keep edge-whitespace rejection where exact retention is unavailable. Empty-cell support must not suppress invalid Ruby/Anno or discard decorations.

Table code requires a context-specific pipe escape. Shared Writer::text(code=true) emits raw code and splits cells on pipe. The independent parser confirms adding one backslash before each pipe preserves that pipe and any existing backslashes. Do not escape all backslashes, substitute entities inside code, or select backtick padding from transformed content. Carry table context through Ruby reading, Anno notes, Concat, Strong/Emphasis and link labels.

Cell Break/Text LF/CR/TAB need explicit representation or rejection. Do not turn a Break into whitespace or a new row. Preserve adjacent-Code rejection across decorations. Every note and reading must survive.

## Lists and ownership

Keep Unordered/Ordered(start), item order/count, None/false/true checkbox and Body ownership. Root's proposed first slice (nonempty list, one nonempty Paragraph per item, multiple Sentences allowed, no nesting) is coherent if unsupported shapes fail explicitly. It covers the three lists in actual00. Actual01 has paragraphs and two RawCode blocks but no table/list constructors, so those manuscripts cannot establish general block coverage.

Ordered U64 exceeds the Markdown marker domain. Test 0, 1, 9, 10, 999999999, 1000000000 and U64MAX. Never clamp or wrap. A maximum valid start with several items must remain valid: only the first marker defines start; reusing a valid marker avoids accidental ten-digit overflow from enumerating later items.

Distinguish absent checkbox, unchecked and checked. Literal initial [x]/[ ] text must remain escaped ordinary text. GFM checkbox semantics involve the first paragraph; do not invent a Paragraph for an empty Body or a nested-first item. The installed parser accepts marker-only/nested-first cases, but its permissiveness does not itself establish preservation of Doc Body semantics.

Multiple Sentences stay one Paragraph with no added punctuation, spaces or line breaks. Test English explicit boundary spaces, Japanese adjacent sentences, mid-Break and decoration-hidden adjacent code. Break continuation indentation depends on marker width plus separator, not universally two spaces; start9/start10 exercise this distinction.

If nested bodies are added later, every continuation line (paragraph, fence, table row) must retain parent indentation. Test parent text before and after child list, mixed list kinds, checked parents and following sibling items; compare AST ownership, not concatenated text.

Blank lines do not separate adjacent same-marker lists. Root's proposed initial rejection is safe. A later representation can alternate markers, but must prove two list nodes remain; a generated comment separator would need an explicit fixed-output contract. Test three adjacent lists and intervening empty/unsupported nodes so invisible output cannot reset adjacency state.

Keep annotated body section_seen guard. Body[Paragraph,List,Section] and Section.body[Paragraph,List] can preserve ownership; Body[Section,List] cannot silently move List under the heading. Do not flatten Paragraph Flow containing Block/Parallel into Sentences. Sections inside items need explicit heading/anchor ownership or rejection. Existing global alias reachability/uniqueness must remain checked.

## Concrete tests to add to the future production change

1. Four alignments, header plus distinct Ruby/Anno/code cells and two rows: exact alignment/row/cell/content events.
2. Header-only positive; headerless and zero-column negatives. Leading/middle/trailing/all empty cells retain counts; whitespace-only is a separate case.
3. Ragged typed or first-CBOR table rejects structurally. Never rely on Markdown padding/truncation.
4. Code pipe, one/two backslashes before pipe, literal entity text, edge backticks, padded code, Unicode; repeat inside annotations and emphasis. Compare exact Code bytes.
5. Mid/edge/consecutive Break and Text controls in cells: explicit supported meaning or failure.
6. Ordered boundary starts including maximum plus multiple items; None/false/true task state and ordinary literal [x].
7. Multi-Sentence item, internal spaces and Break; empty Body, empty list, multi-block, nested/RawCode/Table/Section item bodies reject in the first slice.
8. Three adjacent lists, different kinds, list-table-list, and section-before/after permutations: exact block ownership.
9. Deep/narrow versus wide shapes, shared DAG appearances, source-less legal values, cancellation and sticky stops. Charge before new width-dependent allocation/iteration, keep one Budget/SourceAdmission and never return partial Markdown as success.

## Executed evidence

Isolated Rust probe uses pinned pulldown-cmark 0.13.4 with ENABLE_TABLES|ENABLE_TASKLISTS. Seventeen handwritten Markdown boundary inputs were parsed; parser-locked.log records actual events, command.json records Cargo exit0, and probe/Cargo.lock identifies dependencies.

Observed: raw code pipe loses the Code and suffix; one added pipe escape preserves it, including existing one/two backslashes. Empty cells and header-only tables retain structure. A zero-table spelling becomes Paragraph. Blank-separated '-' lists combine; '-' then '*' yields two lists. Nine-digit start and zero are lists, ten-digit start becomes Paragraph. Checkbox-only/nested-first acceptance is recorded as parser behavior, not Doc compatibility. Explicit continuation indent preserves a hard break and a second paragraph under ordered start10.

The first PowerShell wrapper returned a nonzero shell status despite full events; the independent locked rerun via subprocess records actual Cargo success. No future implementation or cross-target success is claimed. Root subsequently selected an explicit /2 capability version and flat-list scope; production review awaits its fixed request.
